KTH7816 Series

## 1 Product Factsheet


Features


- 16-bit resolution absolute angle output


- High precision (< ±0.35° accuracy error)


- Suitable for on-axis and off-axis non-contact scenarios


- Ultra-low latency (1 μs data updates)


- SPI communication: angle reading, register read / write


- SSI communication: angle reading


- Programmable 4-4096 steps / turn ABZ output


- PWM 14-bit angle output


- Noise as low as of 0.015°


- Built-in programmable memory (MTP)


- Magnetic field strength diagnosis / alarm


- Operating voltage: 3.3V to 5.5V


- Operating temperature range: -40°C to 125°C


- QFN-16L package: 3mm × 3mm and SOP-8 4.9mm × 6mm


Presentation


The KTH7816 Series is a high-precision absolute angle Hall sensor chip
offering up to 16-bit resolution for accurate angle measurements in both
on-axis and off-axis configurations. Capable of handling rotational speeds
ranging from 0 to 120,000 rpm, the KTH7816 Series ensures rapid and
precise angle output, making it a robust choice for applications requiring
accurate angle measurement and speed control.


The KTH7816 Series provides multiple flexible angle output modes to meet
diverse application needs. First, it supports a programmable ABZ quadrature pulse output with up to 4096 steps per revolution, delivering highresolution position data. Additionally, the 4-wire SPI interface facilitates
efficient angle reading and device communication. The KTH7816 Series
also supports a 2-wire SSI output, simplifying system design and integration.


To further enhance its practical application, the KTH7816 Series features
built-in magnetic field strength detection. Users can program high and low
magnetic field thresholds, enabling real-time monitoring and adjustment.
This functionality helps to select the optimal magnet and determine the
appropriate installation setup, ensuring stable operation.


Moreover, the KTH7816 Series incorporates Memory-Programmable Technology (MPT) to store critical configuration parameters. Users can save


5 of 35



